  "tagline": "Postgres extension that mirrors tables into Iceberg columnstores for real-time analytics via DuckDB.",
  "description": "pg_mooncake adds real-time analytics to PostgreSQL by maintaining a columnstore mirror of regular Postgres tables in Apache Iceberg, fed by the moonlink engine with sub-second freshness for inserts, updates and deletes. Analytical queries run through DuckDB (it is now a sub-extension of pg_duckdb), while other engines can read the Iceberg tables directly. Databricks acquired Mooncake Labs in October 2025 to strengthen its Postgres-based Lakebase, and the public repo has seen almost no activity since, so treat it as promising technology with an uncertain open-source future.",
